sequenceDiagram
    title Execution flow — REPL cadence (precise Rust facade signatures)

    participant Initiator as ::main (cli REPL entrypoint)
    participant User as User (terminal)
    participant Watcher as Watcher<br/>::watch (OS callback thread + channel)
    participant Sess as Session<br/>::session_v4::CompilerSession

    Note over Initiator, Sess: † marks proposed/target API not yet in current code.<br/>Receiver (&self / &mut self) is implicit in the lifeline.<br/>Compilation internals (Sched, Cache, Backend, etc.) delegated to exec-flow-compilation —<br/>this diagram shows REPL orchestration around register_module + wait_for_inmem_codegen + eval + trampoline.<br/>Display formatting (format_eval_result, pretty_print, write_prompt, print_banner) is a method group on Sess —<br/>not a separate facade.

    rect rgb(245, 230, 255)
        Note over Initiator, Sess: STARTUP — parse cli args, construct session, register entry module (no wait), init watcher, print banner<br/>(entry module in-mem catches up at the first iteration's wait_for_inmem_codegen.<br/>Other transitively imported modules — including any prelude — are pulled in via the import branch of exec-flow-compilation.<br/>The REPL never references the prelude directly.)

        Initiator ->> Initiator: ::main::parse_args() -> Result<(Action, ProjectTarget, SessionSettings), CliError>
        Note over Initiator: per repl/spec.md §0 — Action ∈ { Repl, Run, Link, Version, Help }.<br/>This diagram covers Action::Repl. For Run / Link see exec-flow-run, exec-flow-link.<br/>ProjectTarget { project_root: PathBuf, entry_module: ModuleFullPath } resolved per repl/spec.md §0.5.

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::new(settings: SessionSettings, project_root: PathBuf) -> CompilerSession
        Note over Sess: spawns priority + nice worker pools — opens cache directory — initialises empty SymbolTables.<br/>Watcher channel opened separately by init_watcher (after register_module, so the entry module's path is known)
        Sess -->> Initiator: CompilerSession

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::register_module(entry_module: &ModuleFullPath) -> Result<(), CranelispError>
        Note over Sess: registers the entry module under target.entry_module (defaults to "user" if no positional arg).<br/>See exec-flow-compilation. Fire-and-forget, returns immediately. Compilation begins in background.
        Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(())

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::init_watcher() -> Result<(), CranelispError>
        Note over Sess: opens the OS file watcher on project_root, wires channel to the background watcher event processor (created suspended)
        Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(())

        Note over Initiator: REPL session state — current_repl_module: ModuleFullPath = target.entry_module<br/>(this is THE module that defns and imports append to. Changeable via /mod. Defaults to entry module.<br/>"user" is just the default name when no positional arg is given — it is not architecturally special.)

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::print_banner(stdout: &mut impl Write)
        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::write_prompt(stdout: &mut impl Write, compile_ms: u64, eval_ms: u64)
    end

    rect rgb(220, 235, 255)
        Note over Initiator, User: LOOP ITERATION — per-input cycle<br/>(repeats until /quit or EOF)

        loop until /quit or EOF
            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 1 — resume watcher processing<br/>(events flow during the prompt-wait window)

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::set_repl_input_active(active: bool) †
            Note over Sess: active=true — Sess background processor pulls events from the watcher channel and invokes re_register_module per event

            Note over Initiator, User: STEP 2 — print prompt and block on user input<br/>(while LineEditor is blocked, watcher events may arrive and be processed concurrently)

            create participant LineEditor as Line editor<br/>::repl::line_editor (rustyline-backed)
            Initiator ->> LineEditor: ::repl::line_editor::read_line(prompt: &str, continuation_state: &mut ContinuationState) -> Result<InputState, ReplError> †
            LineEditor ->> User: display prompt (per repl/spec.md §2.1)

            opt one or more file changes arrive during the prompt-wait
                loop each event (concurrent with LineEditor blocking)
                    Watcher -->> Sess: notify::Event { kind: Modify, paths: [m.cl] } (channel send from OS callback thread)
                    Note over Sess: background watcher processor pulls the event and invokes re_register_module —<br/>typecheck + JIT proceed without blocking the LineEditor read
                    Sess ->> Sess: CompileScheduler::re_register_module(module: &ModuleFullPath) -> bool
                    Note over Sess: see exec-flow-compilation watcher branch
                end
            end

            User ->> LineEditor: keystrokes + Enter
            opt parens unbalanced AND input does not start with "/" (slash commands are single-line per main.rs)
                LineEditor -->> Initiator: InputState::NeedContinuation(partial: String)
                Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::parens_balanced(input: &str) -> bool
                Sess -->> Initiator: false
                loop until balanced
                    Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::write_continuation_prompt(stdout, compile_ms, eval_ms)
                    Initiator ->> LineEditor: ::repl::line_editor::read_line(continuation_prompt, &mut state) †
                    LineEditor ->> User: display continuation prompt (per repl/spec.md §2.2)
                    User ->> LineEditor: keystrokes + Enter
                end
            end
            LineEditor -->> Initiator: InputState::Complete(source: String)

            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 3 — suspend watcher processing<br/>(events arriving from now on accumulate in the channel until next iteration's STEP 1)

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::set_repl_input_active(false) †
            Note over Sess: active=false — Sess background processor stops pulling events —<br/>any in-flight re_register_module calls complete normally

            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 4 — catch up in-mem codegen<br/>(blocks until entry module initial load + all watcher-triggered reloads from STEP 2 are in-mem.<br/>This makes /list, /info, eval all see consistent module state.)

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::wait_for_inmem_codegen() -> Result<(), CranelispError> †
            Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(())

            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 5 — dispatch input via process_commands

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::process_commands(input: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write) -> CommandResult
            Note over Sess: process_commands handles slash commands directly (writing some output to stdout for streaming commands) —<br/>routes /quit to CommandResult::Quit, blank/comment to CommandResult::Nothing,<br/>/list /info /sig /exports etc. to CommandResult::Final(text) via introspection accessors,<br/>Cranelisp source to CommandResult::Compile(src) for the caller to feed into eval.
            Sess -->> Initiator: CommandResult { Nothing | Quit | Final(text: String) | Compile(src: String) }

            alt CommandResult::Nothing
                Note over Initiator: no display, no eval — proceed to STEP 7
            else CommandResult::Quit
                Note over Initiator: break out of loop — see SHUTDOWN below
            else CommandResult::Final(text)
                Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::pretty_print(form: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write)
                Note over Sess: writes the slash-command's output to stdout
            else CommandResult::Compile(src)
                Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::eval(src: &str) -> Result<Option<EvalResult>, CranelispError>

                Note over Sess: eval internals (per pipeline-v4 §6.2 + Decision 44 amended FIXME 0167; 2026-05-13 third amendment) —<br/>parse src, classify each form, route through CompilerSession::process_cluster (the SAME shared orchestrator used by the compilation worker — see exec-flow-compilation typecheck-phase cluster body and facades/int.md "process_cluster — the cluster-atomic orchestration loop").<br/>A non-(begin) REPL input becomes a one-form cluster (per FIXME 0165 — non-(begin)-grouped REPL inputs are processed as single-form clusters, cross-input forward references are NOT supported). A (begin form₁ ... formN) input is the explicit multi-form cluster boundary — eval unwraps the top-level begin and passes the inner forms to process_cluster.<br/>process_cluster constructs SymbolTableAccess::Cluster with modules + staging (&mut empty_staging) + current_module, and threads &mut ctx through a single cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms call. Typecheck mutates staging via ctx.current_symbol_table_mut — the same accessor used in committed-mode. check_forms internally drives Pass 1 then Pass 2 across all parsed entries; the two-pass discipline lives inside check_forms's frame. process_cluster catches ExpansionError::Gap or CheckError::Gap returns from frontend and typecheck, dispatches via handle_gap (register + wait_for_typecheck_symbol + (priority_boost + wait_for_inmem) + wait_for_typecheck_type as needed), and retries the whole check_forms call against a fresh staging frame until expand and check_forms succeed.<br/>For definition clusters, eval follows up with insert_cluster to drain staging atomically into current_repl_module's live SymbolTable — Decision 44 — staging dissolves with the function frame on any failure, drains atomically on success.<br/>For the trailing expression, eval skips insert_cluster — the temp closure has no module commit — and hands the typed AST to a fresh per-eval JITModule.

                opt one or more definition forms (defn / defmacro / deftype / deftrait / impl / import / mod / platform / def) — wrapped as a one-form cluster, or unwrapped from (begin ...) as an explicit multi-form cluster
                    Sess ->> Sess: CompilerSession::process_cluster(forms: Vec[Sexp], scope: &current_repl_module) -> Result<ProcessedCluster, CranelispError> †
                    Note over Sess: shared entry point — invokes the same expand → build_form → single check_forms call (internal Pass 1 then Pass 2) sequence shown in exec-flow-compilation typecheck-phase cluster body — S66 FIXME 0156 build_form returns Vec[ParsedEntry]; Decision 44 amended FIXME 0167 + 2026-05-13 third amendment: typecheck is a single cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms(Vec[ParsedEntry], &mut SymbolTableAccess, &SymbolTables) -> Result[(), CheckError] call — including the gap-orchestration retry loop (whole-cluster retry against fresh staging) for any FQ refs the input touches. scope = current_repl_module supplies typecheck visibility (locals + imports + private symbols). No live commit yet — staging held under &mut borrow inside SymbolTableAccess::Cluster carries the cluster's entries.
                    Sess -->> Sess: ProcessedCluster { drained staging entries, resolved import bindings, populated introspection } †

                    Sess ->> Sess: CompilerSession::insert_cluster(processed: ProcessedCluster, target: &current_repl_module) †
                    Note over Sess: cluster-atomic commit — drains staging into ST_current via SymbolTable::insert_or_update per entry.<br/>Triggers any pending typecheck waiters and (for entries that need_codegen) enqueues per-symbol Jit work items.
                    create participant ST_current as ST[current_repl_module]<br/>cranelisp_types::module::SymbolTable<Code, ()>
                    Sess ->> ST_current: SymbolTable::insert_or_update(sym: Symbol, entry: ModuleEntry<Code>)

                    opt needs_codegen
                        Sess ->> Sess: CompileScheduler::wait_for_inmem(fq: &FQSymbol) †
                        Note over Sess: per-symbol wait — block only on the new symbol's jit, not on every pending in-mem item (global wait already happened at STEP 4)
                    end

                    Sess ->> ST_current: SymbolTable::get(name: &Symbol) -> Option<&ModuleEntry<Code>>
                    ST_current -->> Sess: Some(&ModuleEntry { kind, scheme, .. })
                    Note over Sess: for defn redefinition — per-symbol reclaim of old Arc<Jit> when previous ModuleEntry's Code is dropped (Decision 41 reclaim semantics; D31 retired — substance amended into D41 at S64 + relocated at S69 Phase 3)
                end

                opt trailing expression form (e.g. "(+ 1 2)" or "factorial 10")
                    Sess ->> Sess: CompilerSession::process_form(wrapped_expr: Sexp, scope: &current_repl_module) -> Result<ProcessedForm, CranelispError> †
                    Note over Sess: same shared entry point and same gap-orchestration retry loop — FQ refs in the expression are resolved by process_form before it returns.<br/>scope = current_repl_module for visibility, no commit target.<br/>The wrapped expression is "(defn __expr [] expr)" but __expr is NOT committed anywhere — no insert_symbol call follows.<br/>The temp closure exists only as a typed AST + per-eval JIT until the trampoline returns and the JIT drops.
                    Sess -->> Sess: ProcessedForm { typed_ast, scheme: Some(_), defined_symbol: Some(__expr), callees, needs_codegen: true } †

                    loop each un-codegenned dependency dep: FQSymbol in callees
                        Sess ->> Sess: CompileScheduler::block_for_macro_codegen(fq: &FQSymbol) -> Result<(), SchedulerError>
                        Note over Sess: enqueues BlockingJitCodegen for dep (priority-boosted) and waits — see exec-flow-compilation
                    end

                    create participant EvalJit as Eval JIT<br/>::session_v4::CompilerSession::eval_jit (fresh JITModule per eval, wrapped in Arc<Jit>)
                    Sess ->> EvalJit: cranelisp_backend::compile_to_module<M: Module>(scope: &current_repl_module, names: &[__expr], symbol_tables: &DashMap[ModuleFullPath, SymbolTable[Code, ()]], introspection: Option<&DashMap[FQSymbol, Introspection]>, module: jit_module) -> Result<(), CompilationError>
                    Note over EvalJit: per pipeline-v4 §6.2 — fresh JITModule per eval call.<br/>Wrapped in Jit newtype whose Drop calls unsafe JITModule::free_memory() (per Decision 41 §"Cranelift evidence"; D31 retired — substance amended into D41 at S64 + relocated at S69 Phase 3).<br/>Temp closure has NO entry in ST_current and NO GOT slot — it is one-shot.<br/>Per Decision 41 (S66 amendment + rollback) backend writes Code::Jit(Arc[Jit]) directly via SymbolTable::write_code AND writes the resulting fn pointer to the entry's GOT slot via got().store_slot(slot, ptr) — the GOT is the post-rollback single source of truth for callable addresses (no sibling fn_ptr field). For the temp-closure case there is no entry / no GOT slot — int reads code_ptr from the populated Jit handle directly.
                    EvalJit -->> Sess: Ok(()) — temp closure code_ptr available via the eval's Jit handle

                    create participant Trampoline as IO Trampoline<br/>::session_v4::CompilerSession::trampoline
                    Sess ->> Trampoline: CompilerSession::trampoline(code_ptr: *const u8, expected_type: &Type) -> Result<EvalValue, RuntimeError>
                    Note over Trampoline: runtime cadence active inside the call —<br/>atomic RC inc/dec, fork-join cells (lenient eval / par bind!),<br/>IO trampoline if expected_type wraps IO _ (see exec-flow-runtime)
                    Trampoline -->> Sess: Ok(EvalValue { repr: i64, ty: Type, heap_root: Option<Arc<HeapRetention>> }) †
                    Note over EvalJit: drop(Jit) — custom Drop calls unsafe JITModule::free_memory() —<br/>__expr's executable memory is reclaimed before the next iteration<br/>(safety holds because the value is fully consumed, GOT was never updated, and fn values are heap closures that go through GOTs not raw ptrs)
                end

                Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(Some(EvalResult { Def { symbol, ty, .. } | Value { repr, ty, .. } }))

                Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::format_eval_result(result: &EvalResult) -> String
                Note over Sess: formats per repl/spec.md §1 — ":Type value — classification — docstring" for definitions, bare ":Type value" for expressions, etc.
                Sess -->> Initiator: formatted text

                Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::pretty_print(text: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write)

                opt result is a definition or structural change
                    Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::regenerate_backing_file() -> Result<(), CranelispError>
                    Note over Sess: per repl/spec.md §15 — persists current_repl_module's accumulated forms to {project_root}/{current_repl_module}.cl
                end
            end

            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 6 — sync watcher set with newly-loaded modules<br/>(imports during eval may have registered new modules — the watcher should now watch their files too)

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::sync_watcher() -> Result<(), CranelispError>

            Note over Initiator, Sess: STEP 7 — print next prompt with timing info from the just-completed iteration

            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::write_prompt(stdout, compile_ms, eval_ms)
        end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 220)
        Note over Initiator, Sess: SHUTDOWN — on /quit or EOF

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::wait_for_object_codegen() -> Result<(), CranelispError> †
        Note over Sess: ensures cache .o + sidecars are written for all touched modules — next REPL session can cache-hit
        Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(()) — all object work drained

        Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::shutdown()
        Note over Sess: signals worker pools to drain + terminate —<br/>closes watcher channel — closes cache directory.

        Note over Initiator: drop(Sess) — per-symbol reclaim chain fires (Decision 41) —<br/>each ModuleEntry::Code drops, Arc<Jit> refcount hits 0,<br/>custom Drop calls unsafe JITModule::free_memory() per symbol (one JITModule per defn under D41 cardinality).

        Initiator ->> User: exit (status 0)
    end
